{# The open-unknowns section, shared by the escalate and module-context #}
{# templates (issue #370). Parameterized by (open-unknown list, heading #}
{# text) so each template passes its own heading. The list arrives in #}
{# ledger order, already joined with the reviewer's resolutions: only #}
{# open records reach it, and a resolved or dismissed record never #}
{# renders. The include owns the render bound — the first five records #}
{# in ledger order, the remainder folded into one count line — the same #}
{# discipline the P19 coverage lines keep, so a unit with forty open #}
{# questions still keeps the section bounded. An empty list contributes #}
{# literally nothing: the template renders byte-for-byte what it #}
{# rendered before any ledger was filed. The body is verbatim-pinned by #}
{# the section suite in src/lib.rs — wording or formatting drift fails #}
{# CI. The section states the analysis's own admitted questions; it #}
{# never says what the translation should do about them. #}
{% macro open_unknowns_section(unknowns, heading) %}
{% if !unknowns.is_empty() %}
## {{ heading }}

The analysis filed these open questions about this function: facts it could
not establish from what it read, each beside the evidence that would settle
it. They are admitted gaps, not tasks — treat them as limits on what is
established about this function, and never fill one in with invention.

{% for unknown in unknowns.iter().take(5) %}
- {{ unknown.question|safe }}
  Required evidence: {{ unknown.required_evidence|safe }}
{% endfor %}
{% if unknowns.len() > 5 %}
(+{{ unknowns.len() - 5 }} more open questions not listed)
{% endif %}

{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
